 While delegated work is active, observe the actual agent checkpoint at least every five minutes: current activity/last action, owned-file changes and any running command, process or external action. This is an observation cadence, not an automatic timeout or termination trigger. When a writer appears stalled, inspect its latest status, actual files and authoritative action state. Ask for its current blocker and checkpoint; do not infer failure from silence or start a second writer on the same files. If work can continue within the same assignment, supply the missing approved input.
 
